   "source": [
    "# Porto Trial 2 Data Bundle: Brief Guide\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook explains the structure of the processed Porto taxi destination-prediction data. The preprocessing output contains a heterogeneous urban graph plus supervised prefix-to-destination examples.\n",
    "\n",
    "Main task: given a partial taxi trajectory prefix and metadata, predict the final destination.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f8840f0c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Bundle contents\n",
    "\n",
    "After extracting `porto_data_bundle_trial3.tar.gz`, the expected structure is approximately:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "porto_data_bundle_trial4/\n",
    "├── hetero_graph.pt\n",
    "├── id_mappings.pkl\n",
    "├── feature_names.json\n",
    "├── preprocess_summary.json\n",
    "├── kaggle_test_prefixes.pt\n",
    "├── supervised_splits_preview.pt\n",
    "├── supervised_shards/\n",
    "│   ├── train/\n",
    "│   ├── val/\n",
    "│   └── test/\n",
    "└── tables/\n",
    "    └── *_preview.csv\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Important files: `hetero_graph.pt` is the PyTorch Geometric graph; `supervised_shards/` contains train/val/test examples; `id_mappings.pkl` maps raw IDs to compact graph node IDs; `feature_names.json` gives node feature names; `preprocess_summary.json` gives counts and settings.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
