    "## 3. Heterogeneous graph structure\n",
    "\n",
    "`hetero_graph.pt` is a `torch_geometric.data.HeteroData` object.\n",
    "\n",
    "Node types:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "region\n",
    "poi\n",
    "road\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Typical edge types:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "(region, taxi_transition, region)\n",
    "(region, rev_taxi_transition, region)\n",
    "(poi, located_in, region)\n",
    "(region, has_poi, poi)\n",
    "(road, intersects, region)\n",
    "(region, has_road, road)\n",
    "(road, connects_to, road)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "`region` means a 250m grid cell in Porto. `poi` means an OpenStreetMap point or area of interest. Polygon POIs are converted to representative points before being assigned to grid cells. `road` means an OSM road segment.\n"
   ]
  },
