   "source": [
    "## 6. Prefix sampling\n",
    "\n",
    "Each usable full trip can produce up to `num_prefix_samples = 5` prefix examples. For a trip with `T` GPS points, prefix lengths are sampled from `2, 3, ..., T-1`. If the trip is too short, all available prefix lengths are used. Multiple examples can share the same `trip_id`, but they have different `prefix_sample_id` and `prefix_len_points`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "08baae1a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Why full trajectories are not stored in training shards\n",
    "\n",
    "The original Kaggle `train.csv` has the complete trajectory in `POLYLINE`. The processed supervised shards keep only the prefix representation and final destination label. This avoids leaking the future path after the prefix and prevents duplicating the same full trip several times. If full GPS visualization is needed later, use `trip_id` to look up the original `POLYLINE` from `train.csv`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3a36dc75",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
